  "text": "This series argues decisions, not syntax. After this one, nine videos answer a hundred and twenty-five of the track's questions, each once: system design in two parts, then API design, databases, concurrency, designing objects, reading code, algorithms, and the AI-allowed round. The Python fundamentals page is left out, because it's syntax. Its design questions are covered under concurrency: threads, processes, async and the global interpreter lock. Every topic page has concept checks, three add challenges that run in the browser, and a bank of a hundred and ten multiple-choice questions covers the whole track. As take-homes faded, the round that grew was design. Next: approaching system design.",
